<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% if title %}{{ title }} — {{ site.title }}{% elif isDaily %}{{ page.date | readableDate }} — {{ site.title }}{% else %}{{ site.title }}{% endif %}</title>
    {#- Link cards (2026-09-23): what a link unfurls into on Bluesky, Discord
        and the rest. linkCard hands back this page's description, its card
        (a daily's or essay's own, the site card for everything else, or none
        if even that failed to render), and the article fields. Rendering
        happens in the linkCards collection, before any page is written, so
        a failed card never ships as a dead URL. Every URL here is absolute
        (site.url carries no trailing slash): scrapers resolve nothing. -#}
    {%- set card = collections.linkCards | linkCard(page.url) -%}
    {#- card.title is the spoiler-stripped one: a card is as public as the feed. #}
    {%- set ogTitle = card.title or title or ((page.date | readableDate) if isDaily else site.title) -%}
    {%- set ogDesc = card.description or description or ((site.intro | replace("\n", " ")) if page.url == "/" else site.description) %}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ ogDesc }}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ site.title }}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="{{ card.type or 'website' }}">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ ogTitle }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ ogDesc }}">
    {%- if card.published %}
    <meta property="article:published_time" content="{{ card.published }}">
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if card.image %}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ site.url }}{{ card.image }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    {%- set ogAlt = card.alt or ogTitle %}
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt }}{% if ogAlt != site.title %} — {{ site.title }}{% endif %}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    {%- endif %}
    {#- Both faces are fetched alongside the stylesheet rather than discovered
        inside it. Silkscreen is 8KB and sets every page's chrome; Alegreya is
        17KB and sets every page's prose. Only the roman is preloaded of each:
        bold and italic are a minority of the glyphs on any page and can arrive
        a beat later, but the roman arriving late IS the flash. -#}
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/silkscreen-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/alegreya-sans-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" href="/feed.xml" title="{{ site.title }}">
  </head>
  {#- Grid pages set `wide: true` in their front matter and let <main> take the
      whole shell; everything else gets the narrower, centred reading column.
      The header and the furniture strips are outside main either way, so they
      never change width as you navigate between the two kinds of page. -#}
  <body{% if wide %} class="wide"{% endif %}>
    <header class="site-header">
      {#- The name is the site button's wordmark (button.js), not set type:
          CHAOS·HAT with the dot at the word boundary. aria-label carries
          the domain for readers and crawlers. -#}
      <a class="site-title" href="/">{{ wordmark | safe }}</a>
      {#- Five equal words (2026-09-11). The shelves used to be promoted as the
          way in, but with one shelf and a home page that already leads
          everywhere, tiering marked nothing. Archive is not here because the
          home page ends in "all posts →" — a second door to the same place.
          Feed lives in the footer: it is the one item that is not a page. -#}
      <nav class="site-nav">
        <a href="/shelf/">games</a>
        {% if collections.essayPages | length %}<a href="/essays/">deep thoughts</a>{% endif %}
        {% if collections.pages | length %}<a href="/about/">about</a>{% endif %}
        <a href="/links/">links</a>
        <a href="/guestbook/">guestbook</a>
        {% if collections.featured | length %}<a href="/best/">best of</a>{% endif %}
      </nav>
    </header>

    {#- Says what the auroras mean. Written in the vault's site.yaml; empty
        renders nothing rather than a placeholder. Home page only — it is an
        introduction, and repeating it above every subject page would nag a
        returning reader. It sits here rather than in index.njk so it stays
        above Now Playing: what the site is, then what is current. Drop the
        url test to show it everywhere. Each line of the yaml block becomes
        its own span so the copy's line breaks survive into HTML. -#}
    {% if site.intro and page.url == "/" %}<p class="site-intro">{% for line in site.intro.split("\n") %}<span>{{ line }}</span>{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}

    {#- Both strips share one explicit shape — label row, items row — rather
        than trusting flex-wrap to land the label above the items, which it
        only did at some widths. -#}
    {% set playing = collections.subjectPages | nowPlaying %}
    {% if playing | length %}
    <div class="now">
      <div class="now-head">
        <span class="now-label">now playing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="now-items">
        {% for item in playing %}
        <a class="now-item" href="/s/{{ item.slug }}/"><span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ item.chipUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ item.title }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {#- The essays signpost. Essays are rare, so recency is the wrong axis —
        the strip exists so a visitor learns the second body of writing is
        there at all, and it is furniture, so it does not go stale between
        essays. The chip is the first cited subject's; an essay that cites
        only tags goes chipless. -#}
    {% set essays = collections.essayPages | sort(true, false, "date") %}
    {% if essays | length %}
    <div class="now essays">
      <div class="now-head">
        <span class="now-label">deep thoughts</span>
        <a class="essays-all" href="/essays/">all →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="now-items">
        {% for e in essays | limit(2) %}
        <a class="now-item" href="{{ e.url }}">{% if e.citedSubjects | length %}<span class="sky" style="background-image:url(/img/sky/{{ e.citedSubjects[0] }}-chip.svg)" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}{{ e.title }}<span class="essay-when">{{ e.date | shortDate }}</span></a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <main>
      {{ content | safe }}
    </main>
    {#- The handle is the domain, so the link doubles as identity: rel="me"
        lets the Bluesky profile verify back to here. Written in the vault's
        site.yaml; empty renders no link rather than a dead one. -#}
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>{{ site.author }}</p>
      {% if site.bluesky %}<p><a href="https://bsky.app/profile/{{ site.bluesky }}" rel="me">bluesky</a></p>{% endif %}
      <p><a href="/feed.xml">feed</a></p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
